WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.620 --> 00:00:04.839
Dear Fellow Scholars, this is Two Minute Papers
with Károly Zsolnai-Fehér.

00:00:04.839 --> 00:00:08.680
This video is not about a paper, but the about
the video series itself.

00:00:08.680 --> 00:00:13.629
I don't do this often, but for the sake of
transparency, I wanted to make sure to tell

00:00:13.629 --> 00:00:14.760
you about this.

00:00:14.760 --> 00:00:19.830
We have recently hit 175.000 subscribers on
the channel!

00:00:19.830 --> 00:00:22.700
I find this number almost unfathomable.

00:00:22.700 --> 00:00:27.580
And please know that this became a possibility
only because of you, so I would like to let

00:00:27.580 --> 00:00:32.329
you know how grateful I am for your support
here on YouTube and Patreon.

00:00:32.329 --> 00:00:36.879
As most of you know, I still work as a full-time
researcher at the Technical University of

00:00:36.879 --> 00:00:41.870
Vienna and I get the question "why not go
full time on Two Minute Papers?"

00:00:41.870 --> 00:00:44.910
from you Fellow Scholars increasingly often.

00:00:44.910 --> 00:00:50.070
The answer is that over time, I would love
to, but our current financial situation does

00:00:50.070 --> 00:00:51.429
not allow it.

00:00:51.429 --> 00:00:52.620
Let me explain that.

00:00:52.620 --> 00:00:58.260
First, I tried the run the channel solely
on YouTube ads, which led to a rude awakening

00:00:58.260 --> 00:01:04.210
- most people (myself included) are very surprised
when they hear that the rates had become so

00:01:04.210 --> 00:01:09.980
low that around the first one million viewer
mark, the series earned less than a dollar

00:01:09.980 --> 00:01:10.980
a day.

00:01:10.980 --> 00:01:16.530
Then, we introduced Patreon, and with your
support, now we are able to buy proper equipment

00:01:16.530 --> 00:01:18.310
to make better videos for you.

00:01:18.310 --> 00:01:23.920
I can, without hesitation, say that you are
the reason this channel can exist.

00:01:23.920 --> 00:01:28.430
Everything is better this way: now we have
two independent revenue sources (Patreon being

00:01:28.430 --> 00:01:33.991
the most important), however, whenever YouTube
or Patreon monetization issues arise, you

00:01:33.991 --> 00:01:37.730
see many other channels disappearing into
the ether.

00:01:37.730 --> 00:01:43.350
I am terrified of this and I want to do everything
I possibly can to make sure that this does

00:01:43.350 --> 00:01:47.790
not happen to us and we can keep running this
series for a long-long time.

00:01:47.790 --> 00:01:54.040
However, if anything happens to any of these
revenue streams, simply put, we are toast.

00:01:54.040 --> 00:01:58.810
Even though it would be a dream come true,
because of this, it would be irresponsible

00:01:58.810 --> 00:02:01.120
to go full time on the papers.

00:02:01.120 --> 00:02:06.720
To remedy this, we have been thinking about
introducing a third revenue stream with sponsorships

00:02:06.720 --> 00:02:09.249
for a small amount of videos each month.

00:02:09.249 --> 00:02:15.739
The majority, 75% of the videos would remain
Patreon supported, and the remaining 25% would

00:02:15.739 --> 00:02:21.540
be sponsored, just enough to enable me and
my wife to do this full time in the future.

00:02:21.540 --> 00:02:26.530
There would be no other changes to the videos,
Patreon supporters get all of them in early

00:02:26.530 --> 00:02:29.959
access, and as before, I choose the papers
too.

00:02:29.959 --> 00:02:33.959
With this, if something happens to any one
of the revenue streams, we would be able to

00:02:33.959 --> 00:02:36.780
keep the series afloat without any delays.

00:02:36.780 --> 00:02:42.239
I would also have more time to every now and
then, fly out and inform key political decision

00:02:42.239 --> 00:02:46.989
makers on the state of AI so they can make
better decisions for us.

00:02:46.989 --> 00:02:51.170
Everything else would remain the same, the
videos would arrive more often in time, and

00:02:51.170 --> 00:02:53.540
the dream could perhaps come true.

00:02:53.540 --> 00:02:58.819
I think transparency is of utmost importance
and wanted to make sure to inform you before

00:02:58.819 --> 00:03:00.319
any change happens.

00:03:00.319 --> 00:03:01.989
I hope you are okay with this.

00:03:01.989 --> 00:03:07.260
And, if you are a company and you are interested
in sponsoring the series, let's talk.

00:03:07.260 --> 00:03:10.789
As always thanks for watching and for your
generous support, and I'll see you next time!

